&lt;p&gt;Interested in learning how Columbia alumni launched their careers in software engineering, product, data, cybersecurity, or other technology roles? Join us for Ask an Alum: Speed Networking, a fast-paced evening designed to help you explore tech pathways through candid conversations with alumni working across the industry. This is a great opportunity to understand real roles, team dynamics, and the skills that matter in early tech careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event Highlights:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alumni Introductions:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hear brief introductions from alumni working in software, product, data, and other tech-driven roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Timed Roundtable Conversations:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Rotate through short, structured conversations with alumni to ask questions, compare paths, and learn about how teams work inside different tech organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Networking:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Connect informally with alumni afterward to continue discussions, seek advice, and expand your Columbia network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
